cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PHON in your research, please cite this repository."
title: "PHON: A Domain-Specific Language for Photonic and Phononic Wave Simulation with Neural Network Inference"
abstract: >-
  PHON is an open-source DSL for wave-based circuit design, supporting both
  photonic (optical) and phononic (acoustic) media through a unified
  declarative syntax. Because linear wave propagation is mathematically
  identical for light and sound, the same DSL source compiles to simulation,
  GDSII layout export, and (as of v0.10.0) neural network inference via
  layer/propagate primitives with numpy-backed matmul. The medium attribute
  dispatches physics constants (refractive index, sound velocity) without
  changing the computation, enabling cross-medium weight transfer.
  v0.10.0 simulates on CPU; physical deployment (photonic chips, SAW devices)
  is future work. A companion pipeline (PHON-LLM, separate repository)
  provides natural-language frontends: 135M LoRA-tuned code generation with
  constrained decoding (98% syntax validity) and hybrid parameter extraction
  (regex + Qwen-0.5B/Outlines CFG, 100% on curated and novel eval sets).
  Phase 5 (v0.10.0) achieves 97.78% MNIST test accuracy with 0 mismatches
  versus scikit-learn predictions on a 100-sample audit set.
